    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao requested <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/bytecodealliance/teams/wasmtime-core-reviewers\">wasmtime-core-reviewers</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632331320,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792172291
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao requested <a href=\"https://github.com/pchickey\">pchickey</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632331321,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792172291
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> rvolosatovs submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#pullrequestreview-5552203030\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I find it quite surprising for GET/HEAD/CONNECT requests to carry a body, in fact I would expect the (default) wasi-http implementation to explicitly reject such requests.</p>\n<p>Could you share a bit more context as to why this would be a desirable feature?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632347002,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792175982
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6222456898\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it's not that get bodies are desirable. today the body is accepted, finish returns ok, and the origin receives none,that's the bug. rejecting is fine with us, but it would also fail ge ts that create a body and write nothing.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632349463,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792176555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6222525728\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the preference is to reject the request, which error code should the <code>handle</code> function return?<br>\nAnd if you’d rather reject it, then you should be the one to handle this task.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632350331,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792176806
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao edited a <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6222525728\">comment</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the preference is to reject the request, which error code should the <code>handle</code> function return?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632351201,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792177042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6274822192\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the preference is to reject the request, which error code should the <code>handle</code> function return?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><code>HTTP-protocol-error</code> perhaps?</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/463701e0f6c575a5d24ae31c2ec1e0ebf09d28e1/proposals/http/wit/types.wit#L71\">https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/463701e0f6c575a5d24ae31c2ec1e0ebf09d28e1/proposals/http/wit/types.wit#L71</a></p>\n<p>Otherwise, we could also just use <code>internal-error</code> with a message I think <a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/463701e0f6c575a5d24ae31c2ec1e0ebf09d28e1/proposals/http/wit/types.wit#L79\">https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/463701e0f6c575a5d24ae31c2ec1e0ebf09d28e1/proposals/http/wit/types.wit#L79</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633102150,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792436057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>.</p>",
        "id": 633292396,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792497328
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6290401785\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Tried the “HTTP protocol error” thing, but with that “/get with body” also fails, since the host can’t really tell whether a body has content. Keep sending for now. Also added a case where a GET body gets created but never written to.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633294312,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792497803
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784#issuecomment-6290572817\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14784\">PR #14784</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So I don't recommend rejecting the request, do you think?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633296363,
